    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #362\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-151-notifications-v1-04-05-deliver-notific-thr_c986iktz3g` pushed to origin successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #151: delivering committed notifications through Web Push and APNs.\n\n- **`writeNotification`** now enqueues one `notificationFanout` graphile-worker job per genuinely-new notification (dedup via `RETURNING id` on the existing `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` insert), keyed by the notification's own id so the job can never be duplicated even if the caller replays.\n- **`notificationFanout` job handler** loads every active `push_subscriptions` registration for the notification's user and dispatches each through its channel's adapter — Web Push (VAPID, via the `web-push` package) or APNs (raw HTTP/2, ES256 provider JWT cached for up to 55 minutes, sandbox/production host selected from `apns_environment`).\n- **`push_deliveries`** (new migration 0032) is the durable per-(notification, registration) dedup key: a unique index on `(notification_id, push_subscription_id)` plus a three-state status (pending/delivered/permanently-failed) guarantees a retried job run never re-sends a pair that already succeeded or was already ruled out.\n- Transient provider/network failures leave the delivery row pending and rethrow so graphile-worker retries the whole job; a permanent rejection (404/410/`BadDeviceToken`) marks that one delivery failed and invalidates only that registration via #150's `revokePushSubscriptionByProviderInvalidation`.\n- Notification payloads sent to providers are limited to `notification_id`, `title`, and `link_href` — no source content beyond the notification row.\n\n## Verification\n\n- TypeScript, ESLint, Prettier, and `dependency-cruiser` boundary checks: all clean\n- Unit tests: 127/127 passed\n- Integration tests: 857/857 passed (74 files), including 8 new tests covering exactly-once fanout, revoked-registration skipping, cross-retry idempotency, partial transient-failure retry, and permanent-failure scoped revocation\n- E2E tests: 5/5 passed\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
