    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #362\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to `bb/relay-151-notifications-v1-04-05-deliver-notific-thr_c986iktz3g` (existing PR #362 branch).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #151: delivering committed notifications through Web Push and APNs.\n\n- **`writeNotification`** enqueues one `notificationFanout` graphile-worker job per genuinely-new notification, keyed by the notification's own id.\n- **`notificationFanout` job handler** loads every active `push_subscriptions` registration for the notification's user and dispatches each through its channel's adapter — Web Push (VAPID) or APNs (HTTP/2, cached ES256 provider JWT, sandbox/production host from `apns_environment`).\n- **`push_deliveries`** (migration 0032) is the durable per-(notification, registration) dedup key guaranteeing exactly-once delivery across job retries.\n- Transient failures retry via graphile-worker; permanent provider rejections (404/410/`BadDeviceToken`) invalidate only the reported registration via #150's invalidation mechanism.\n- Payloads to providers are limited to `notification_id`, `title`, and `link_href`.\n\n## Review fixes (this update)\n\nFixed the last open finding from the latest automated review round: `writeNotification`'s `client.query()` call was untyped, with a downstream `rows[0] as { id: string } | undefined` cast that performed no compile-time check — the same any-at-boundary pattern already fixed elsewhere in this PR. Now uses `client.query<{ id: string }>(...)`.\n\n(All prior review rounds' findings — duplicated APNs alert body, missing request timeout, HTTP/2 client-level socket leak, untyped DB rows in `notificationsStore.ts`/`pushDeliveriesStore.ts`, unchecked APNs response cast, unbounded response accumulation — were already fixed and confirmed resolved by CI.)\n\n## Verification\n\n- TypeScript, ESLint, Prettier, and `dependency-cruiser` boundary checks: all clean\n- Unit tests: 127/127 passed\n- Integration tests: 857/857 passed (74 files), including 8 tests covering exactly-once fanout, revoked-registration skipping, cross-retry idempotency, partial transient-failure retry, and permanent-failure scoped revocation\n- E2E tests: 5/5 passed\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
